.TH "ironstate" "1" "" "TacoContent" "Declarative task runner"
.SH NAME
ironstate \- declarative, Ansible\-style task runner driven by YAML
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]ironstate\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] [\f[I]COMMAND\f[R]]
.PP
\f[B]ironstate\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]ironstate\f[R] reconciles desired system state declared in YAML
playbooks.
It evaluates each task, reports what would change by default, and
applies changes only when \f[B]\(enapply\f[R] is specified.
.PP
The program is distributed as a single binary for Windows, Linux, and
macOS.
A playbook may contain built\-in handlers and external handlers supplied
by installed Go plugins.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enplaybook\f[R]=\f[I]PATH\f[R]
Path to the site or main YAML document.
The value may be an existing file, a playbook directory, or a bare name.
Directories are searched for \f[B]site.yml\f[R], \f[B]site.yaml\f[R],
\f[B]main.yml\f[R], and \f[B]main.yaml\f[R].
Defaults to the current directory.
.TP
\f[B]\(envars\-file\f[R]=\f[I]PATH\f[R]
Merge an additional variables document after the automatic host and
platform overlays.
May be repeated; later files take precedence.
.TP
\f[B]\(envar\f[R]=\f[I]KEY=VALUE\f[R]
Override a variable by dotted path.
May be repeated and has the highest variable precedence.
.TP
\f[B]\(enapply\f[R]
Apply changes.
Without this option, ironstate performs a dry run except for read\-only
fact gathering and validation operations.
.TP
\f[B]\(entags\f[R]=\f[I]TAG[,TAG\&...]\f[R]
Restrict processing to tasks or actions carrying one of the specified
tags.
.TP
\f[B]\(enoutput\f[R]=\f[I]FORMAT\f[R]
Select result output format: \f[B]table\f[R] (the default) or
\f[B]json\f[R].
JSON results are written to standard output; operational messages are
written to standard error.
.TP
\f[B]\-v\f[R], \f[B]\(enverbose\f[R]
Print additional information for skipped or already\-satisfied tasks.
.TP
\f[B]\(enno\-color\f[R]
Disable colored terminal output.
.TP
\f[B]\(enallow\-plugin\-install\f[R]
Allow plugins declared by the playbook to be installed automatically.
This downloads and executes third\-party code and is separate from
\f[B]\(enapply\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\(enhelp\f[R]
Show command help.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS version
Show the ironstate version, commit, and build date.
.SS init [PLAYBOOK\-NAME]
Create a minimal playbook directory structure.
Existing files and directories are not overwritten.
.TP
\f[B]\(enscan\f[R]
Populate the generated playbook from handlers that support system
scanning.
.SS filters list
List built\-in and discovered script filters.
.TP
\f[B]\(endir\f[R]=\f[I]PATH\f[R]
Directory to scan for external script filters.
Defaults to \f[B]filters\f[R].
.SS doctor
Check command availability, discovered script filters, and optionally
validate plugins used by a playbook.
.TP
\f[B]\(enfilters\-dir\f[R]=\f[I]PATH\f[R]
Directory to scan for external script filters.
Defaults to \f[B]filters\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\(enplaybook\f[R]=\f[I]PATH\f[R]
Validate declared plugins and qualified handler names in the specified
playbook.
.SS plugin
Manage external handler plugins.
Plugins are installed in a per\-user cache and communicate with
ironstate over a versioned gRPC protocol.
.SS plugin install ORGANIZATION.PLUGIN[\(atVERSION]
Install a plugin from its Go module.
The module convention is:
.IP
.EX
github.com/ORGANIZATION/ironstate\-handler\-NAME
.EE
.PP
If no version is supplied, \f[B]latest\f[R] is used.
.SS plugin list
List installed plugins, versions, handlers, and summaries.
.SS plugin info ORGANIZATION.PLUGIN
Display installed plugin manifests, including source, checksum, license,
protocol version, and handlers.
.SS plugin update ORGANIZATION.PLUGIN[\(atVERSION]
Install an updated version while retaining older cached versions.
Use \f[B]\(enall\f[R] to update every installed plugin.
.SS plugin uninstall ORGANIZATION.PLUGIN[\(atVERSION]
Remove one installed plugin version.
Without a version, remove all installed versions of the plugin.
.SS plugin test ORGANIZATION.PLUGIN
Invoke a plugin handler without loading a full playbook.
.TP
\f[B]\(enhandler\f[R]=\f[I]NAME\f[R]
Handler name to invoke.
.TP
\f[B]\(enitem\f[R]=\f[I]YAML\-OR\-JSON\f[R]
Handler item as a YAML or JSON mapping.
.TP
\f[B]\(enapply\f[R]
Run the install or uninstall operation after testing.
.SS plugin bench ORGANIZATION.PLUGIN
Benchmark a plugin handler operation and emit JSON timing statistics.
.TP
\f[B]\(enhandler\f[R]=\f[I]NAME\f[R]
Handler name to benchmark.
.TP
\f[B]\(enitem\f[R]=\f[I]YAML\-OR\-JSON\f[R]
Handler item as a YAML or JSON mapping.
.TP
\f[B]\(enoperation\f[R]=\f[I]OPERATION\f[R]
Operation to benchmark: \f[B]test\f[R], \f[B]describe\f[R],
\f[B]install\f[R], or \f[B]uninstall\f[R].
Defaults to \f[B]test\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\(eniterations\f[R]=\f[I]N\f[R]
Number of operation calls.
Defaults to 10.
.TP
\f[B]\(enapply\f[R]
Permit mutating install or uninstall operations.
.SH PLAYBOOK FORMAT
A playbook is a YAML document containing variables and tasks:
.IP
.EX
vars:
  editor: vim

tasks:
  \- name: Ensure a package is installed
    apt:
      name: git
      state: present
.EE
.PP
Tasks may be placed directly in the main document or loaded through the
playbook hierarchy.
The hierarchy supports \f[B]hosts/\f[R], \f[B]variables/\f[R],
\f[B]roles/\f[R], \f[B]packages/\f[R], and \f[B]tasks/\f[R] directories.
Host and variable overlays may be selected using hostname, operating
system family, platform, and architecture facts.
.PP
A playbook may declare external plugins:
.IP
.EX
plugins:
  \- use: acme.hosts\(atv1.2.3

tasks:
  \- name: Ensure a hosts entry
    acme.hosts.ensure_entry:
      path: /etc/hosts
      ip: 10.0.0.12
      hostname: build.local
.EE
.PP
A missing plugin is reported with the installation command.
Automatic installation requires \f[B]\(enallow\-plugin\-install\f[R].
An optional \f[B]ironstate.lock.yaml\f[R] file pins plugin versions and
checksums.
.PP
Built\-in handlers are available under their normal names and under the
namespaced aliases \f[B]ironstate.builtin.NAME\f[R].
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[B]ironstate.yaml\f[R], \f[B].ironstate.yaml\f[R]
Optional configuration file in the current working directory.
Command\-line flags take precedence.
.TP
\f[B].env\f[R], \f[B].secrets\f[R]
Optional environment files loaded from the current working directory.
Secret values from \f[B].secrets\f[R] are masked in later output.
.TP
\f[B]ironstate.lock.yaml\f[R]
Optional playbook lockfile containing plugin versions and checksums.
.TP
\f[B]$XDG_CACHE_HOME/ironstate/plugins/\f[R]
Plugin cache on systems following the XDG convention.
On Windows, the platform user cache directory is used.
.SH OUTPUT
Table output is intended for interactive use.
JSON output is intended for automation:
.IP
.EX
ironstate \-\-playbook site.yml \-\-output json | jq
.EE
.PP
Each JSON result includes the module, package, state, action, apply
status, failure status, execution result, and \f[B]duration_ms\f[R]
timing.
.PP
Messages, progress, warnings, and plugin logs are written to standard
error so that standard output remains machine\-readable when JSON output
is selected.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
The run completed without an unhandled task failure.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
The run stopped because of an unhandled task failure or dispatch error.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R]
The playbook could not be loaded or parsed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[B]NO_COLOR\f[R], \f[B]IRONSTATE_NO_COLOR\f[R]
Disable colored output.
.TP
\f[B]IRONSTATE_\f[R]*
Configuration values may be supplied through environment variables using
the corresponding configuration key with the \f[B]IRONSTATE_\f[R]
prefix.
.SH EXAMPLES
Dry run a playbook:
.IP
.EX
ironstate \-\-playbook playbooks/site
.EE
.PP
Apply changes:
.IP
.EX
ironstate \-\-playbook playbooks/site \-\-apply
.EE
.PP
Apply only selected tags:
.IP
.EX
ironstate \-\-playbook playbooks/site \-\-tags security,packages \-\-apply
.EE
.PP
Use variable overrides:
.IP
.EX
ironstate \-\-playbook site.yml \-\-vars\-file ci.yml \-\-var editor=vim \-\-var ssh.port=2222
.EE
.PP
Validate a playbook\(cqs plugins:
.IP
.EX
ironstate doctor \-\-playbook site.yml
.EE
.PP
Install and test an external handler:
.IP
.EX
ironstate plugin install acme.hosts\(atv1.2.3
ironstate plugin test acme.hosts \-\-handler ensure_entry \-\-item \(aq{\(dqpath\(dq:\(dq/tmp/hosts\(dq,\(dqip\(dq:\(dq10.0.0.12\(dq,\(dqhostname\(dq:\(dqbuild.local\(dq}\(aq
.EE
